Milestone 1 Phase E - button bring-up and event classification
Waveshare ESP32-S3-LCD-2.8 (SKU 30223, non-touch) - 2026-08-03

Captured from the native USB Serial/JTAG console at 115200 baud.
Firmware: hardware-validation profile, git 425ad5a12650, dirty=true
(Phase E work uncommitted at capture time).

Normalisation applied to this file, and nothing else:
  - ANSI colour escapes removed
  - CR removed and trailing whitespace stripped, so the file is LF-only
  - ESP-IDF Verbose-level lines (prefix 'V') dropped: SPI bus-lock and
    polling-transaction plumbing from the concurrently running display
    pattern cycle, which repeats hundreds of times per minute and is
    unrelated to the button. Debug, Info, Warning and Error kept in full.

No device MAC address, serial number, host path or username appears in this
file (Bootstrap Spec 16.8). The esptool output used to prove download-mode
entry is summarised below rather than pasted, because esptool prints the MAC.

==============================================================================
PART 1 - clean boot, button untouched

Shows the accepted ordering: the boot report and phase=ready complete BEFORE
the button GPIO is configured, and 20 s of an untouched line classify nothing.
