==============================================================================
PART 3 - ROM download loader reached by holding BOOT across a power cycle

Passive capture (no DTR/RTS asserted). Proves manual BOOT recovery works, and
that the download-mode latch survives resets - only a power cycle clears it.
==============================================================================
ESP-ROM:esp32s3-20210327
Build:Mar 27 2021
rst:0x15 (USB_UART_CHIP_RESET),boot:0x22 (DOWNLOAD(USB/UART0))
Saved PC:0x40041a76
waiting for download

esptool cross-checks, summarised (raw output withheld: it prints the MAC):
  - 'chip_id' with auto-reset, IO0 configured as an application input:
    connected, ESP32-S3 (QFN56) rev v0.2, USB mode USB-Serial/JTAG,
    stub uploaded and running. Flashing needs no button press.
  - 'chip_id --before no_reset --after no_reset' after the BOOT power cycle:
    connected and reported 'Staying in bootloader'. This succeeds only if the
    chip is already in the loader, so BOOT entry is confirmed.
  - 'run' did NOT leave the loader; the board re-reported boot:0x22.
    A USB-C power cycle without BOOT held was required.

==============================================================================
PART 4 - after the download-mode excursion

Power cycle without BOOT held booted straight into the application, which also
proves IO0 is not held low by a stuck contact. 3 further taps classify cleanly.
